// Playing live and sharing
// A live set grows and shrinks one
// layer at a time. Here every layer
// is muted with _$: but the kick.
//
// Try: play, then unmute one layer
// at a time, with an Update each
// time. Then mute them one by one.

setcpm(31)
$: s("bd*4")
_$: s("~ cp").room(0.3)
_$: s("hh*8").gain(0.4)
_$: note("<c2 c2 ab1 bb1>")
  .s("sawtooth").lpf(500)
_$: n("<0 2 4 7>*4")
  .scale("C4:minor").s("piano")
// ---
// Recording your track
// ⋮ then Export audio saves the music
// as a WAV file: pick the first and
// the last cycle, and where it goes.
//
// Try: export 8 cycles of this.

setcpm(31)
$: arrange([4, s("bd*4")],
  [4, s("bd*4, hh*8")])
$: note("<c2 ab1>").s("sawtooth")
  .lpf(500)
// ---
// Sharing
// ⋮ then Share sends the code as text
// to another app. Copy web link makes
// a link that plays it in a web
// browser; Import shared link opens
// such a link from the clipboard.
//
// Try: share this code with a friend.

setcpm(31)
$: s("bd*2 [~ bd] sd ~, hh*8")
// ---
// MIDI
// .midi() sends notes to a synth or a
// keyboard, over USB or Bluetooth.
// ⋮ then MIDI devices lists them.
//
// Try, with a device connected:
// uncomment the last line, Update.

setcpm(31)
$: note("c3 eb3 g3 bb3").s("piano")
// $: note("c3 eb3 g3 bb3").midi()
// ---
// Keep going
// You know the basics. The Examples
// of the Library are songs to pull
// apart, and the Reference has every
// function with examples. Tap + in
// the Library to start a project of
// your own. Have fun!

setcpm(31)
$: s("bd*2 [~ bd] sd ~, hh*8")
$: note("<c2 ab1 bb1 g1>")
  .s("sawtooth").lpf(600)
